 ; --- the RANDOM stop: seven placeholders, then the pick itself ---------------
 ; The wall above holds the whole cast, so this last row exists only to give
 ; RANDOM a cursor stop. skipslot cells are never drawn and never take the
 ; cursor; searchemptyboxesdown (in [Select Info]) walks right along this row,
 ; so pressing down anywhere on the wall lands on RANDOM. start.lua draws the
 ; randomselect slot as a label centred under the wall, not as a portrait cell.
skipslot
skipslot
skipslot
skipslot
skipslot
skipslot
skipslot
randomselect

